### Try these from VS Code (REST Client extension), Rider or Visual Studio.
@host = http://localhost:5102

### Stores
GET {{host}}/api/inventory/stores

### Stock for a store
GET {{host}}/api/inventory/stores/STORE-001/stock

### Low stock only
GET {{host}}/api/inventory/stores/STORE-001/stock?lowOnly=true

### Manual adjustment (e.g. damaged goods)
POST {{host}}/api/inventory/stores/STORE-001/stock/BC-JKT-001/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "delta": -1, "reason": "Damaged - torn seam" }

### Handheld sync: push offline mutations (send twice - second time is idempotent)
POST {{host}}/api/inventory/sync/push
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storeId": "STORE-001",
  "deviceId": "TC52-0042",
  "mutations": [
    { "mutationId": "6a1f3c1e-6a5b-4a4e-9a51-0a4b2b4b1a01", "type": "StockCount", "sku": "BC-BOOT-001", "quantity": 12, "occurredAt": "2026-11-09T10:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### Handheld sync: pull everything (since=0), then pass the returned checkpoint
GET {{host}}/api/inventory/sync/pull?storeId=STORE-001&since=0

### Audit trail
GET {{host}}/api/inventory/stores/STORE-001/movements?take=20
